00:13:34.320 --> 00:13:38.430
the protocols and systems
that we have as players now

00:13:38.430 --> 00:13:42.586
in comparison to, you
know, the early 2000's

00:13:42.586 --> 00:13:46.138
the early 2010's is way different.

00:13:46.138 --> 00:13:46.971
Is it?

00:13:46.971 --> 00:13:51.150 position:61%
Way different in terms of even not only

00:13:51.150 --> 00:13:54.510 position:66%
the processes, but in terms of the culture

00:13:54.510 --> 00:13:57.570
in and around concussion
is totally different.

00:13:57.570 --> 00:14:01.930
So I started playing
rugby in 2006 at my school

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:05.563
and probably from about 2006

00:14:05.563 --> 00:14:09.326
to about 2013, 14 or so,

00:14:09.326 --> 00:14:13.170
what I experienced was
the culture within rugby

00:14:13.170 --> 00:14:17.100
that the concussion wasn't
really seen as a serious injury.

00:14:17.100 --> 00:14:20.400
So if someone was to,
you know, get concussed

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:24.300
or get knocked out on the
field, it was almost seen

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:28.350
